      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T23:02:32.932508Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:1/seg:0",
      "source": "POSIX defines a portable timer interface built on arbitrary clock IDs:",
      "source_hash": 5320965430932246167,
      "context_hash": 11251418120054691644,
      "translation": "POSIX는 임의의 클록 ID를 기반으로 하는 이식 가능한 타이머 인터페이스를 정의합니다:",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "POSIX": "POSIX",
        "timer": "타이머"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T23:02:32.932508Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:3/seg:0",
      "source": "Notification modes",
      "source_hash": 18316839447398800778,
      "context_hash": 7546751460772610256,
      "translation": "알림 모드",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T23:02:32.932508Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:2/block:0/seg:0",
      "source": "clock_nanosleep",
      "source_hash": 539774280394213408,
      "context_hash": 17767252203305139886,
      "translation": "clock_nanosleep",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T23:02:32.932508Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:2/block:1/seg:0",
      "source": "`clock_nanosleep` suspends the calling thread until an absolute or relative time:",
      "source_hash": 3038477784856234550,
      "context_hash": 6995950450849340160,
      "translation": "`clock_nanosleep`은 호출한 스레드를 절대 시각 또는 상대 시간까지 일시 중단합니다:",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T23:02:32.932508Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:2/block:3/seg:0",
      "source": "The absolute form is important for precise periodic loops — avoids drift from relative sleep accumulation.",
      "source_hash": 923814002150665792,
      "context_hash": 9027070157283879886,
      "translation": "절대 시각 형식은 정밀한 주기적 루프에 중요합니다 — 상대 sleep이 누적되면서 생기는 드리프트(drift)를 방지합니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T23:02:32.932509Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:2/block:4/seg:0",
      "source": "Precise periodic loop",
      "source_hash": 14534147505882212267,
      "context_hash": 10466676746195819459,
      "translation": "정밀한 주기적 루프",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T23:02:32.932509Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:3/block:0/seg:0",
      "source": "timerfd",
      "source_hash": 15066115547053594119,
      "context_hash": 10895166713334565439,
      "translation": "timerfd",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T23:02:32.932509Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:3/block:1/seg:0",
      "source": "`timerfd_create` returns a file descriptor that becomes readable when the timer expires.",
      "source_hash": 249830780369748336,
      "context_hash": 494883808522031789,
      "translation": "`timerfd_create`는 타이머가 만료되면 읽기 가능 상태가 되는 파일 디스크립터를 반환합니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "file descriptor": "파일 디스크립터",
        "timer": "타이머"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T23:02:32.932509Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:3/block:1/seg:1",
      "source": "This enables integrating timers with `epoll` and `select` — no signals needed.",
      "source_hash": 3221440163268206634,
      "context_hash": 10592804487480571283,
      "translation": "이를 통해 타이머를 `epoll` 및 `select`와 통합할 수 있습니다 — 시그널이 필요하지 않습니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "timers": "타이머"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T23:02:32.932509Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:3/block:3/seg:0",
      "source": "timerfd_settime flags",
      "source_hash": 17743735172331755490,
      "context_hash": 2579758805076999706,
      "translation": "timerfd_settime 플래그",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T23:02:32.932510Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:4/block:0/seg:0",
      "source": "Kernel implementation",
      "source_hash": 289839300155434675,
      "context_hash": 11641434508547434145,
      "translation": "커널 구현",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "kernel": "커널"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T23:02:32.932510Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:4/block:1/seg:0",
      "source": "POSIX timers in the kernel",
      "source_hash": 18009544367177179271,
      "context_hash": 1756355379053567625,
      "translation": "커널의 POSIX 타이머",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "POSIX": "POSIX",
        "kernel": "커널",
        "timers": "타이머"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T23:02:32.932510Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:4/block:3/seg:0",
      "source": "Each `timer_create()` allocates a `k_itimer` backed by an `hrtimer`.",
      "source_hash": 11402486173621726225,
      "context_hash": 12373157840091341126,
      "translation": "각 `timer_create()`는 `hrtimer`를 기반으로 하는 `k_itimer`를 할당합니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T23:02:32.932510Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:4/block:3/seg:1",
      "source": "When the hrtimer fires, it queues the signal.",
      "source_hash": 16918285975178323049,
      "context_hash": 13775637048605090452,
      "translation": "hrtimer가 만료되면 시그널을 큐에 넣습니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "hrtimer": "hrtimer",
        "queue": "큐"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T23:02:32.932510Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:4/block:4/seg:0",
      "source": "timerfd in the kernel",
      "source_hash": 2051240534127520980,
      "context_hash": 15690882123769739263,
      "translation": "커널의 timerfd",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "kernel": "커널"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T23:02:32.932510Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:5/block:0/seg:0",
      "source": "Overruns",
      "source_hash": 15929839691084925897,
      "context_hash": 15977579511984944079,
      "translation": "오버런",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T23:02:32.932510Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:5/block:1/seg:0",
      "source": "When a periodic timer fires faster than you consume it, expirations accumulate:",
      "source_hash": 11415536733621777224,
      "context_hash": 16345956746277648554,
      "translation": "주기적 타이머가 소비하는 속도보다 빠르게 만료되면 만료 횟수가 누적됩니다:",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "timer": "타이머"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T23:02:32.932510Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:5/block:3/seg:0",
      "source": "Overruns happen when:",
      "source_hash": 8800646892677639739,
      "context_hash": 6379220856699835969,
      "translation": "오버런이 발생하는 경우:",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T23:02:32.932510Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:5/block:4/seg:0",
      "source": "Handler takes longer than the period",
      "source_hash": 9501177307813536797,
      "context_hash": 4265167113425599240,
      "translation": "핸들러 실행 시간이 주기보다 긴 경우",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "handler": "핸들러"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T23:02:32.932510Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:5/block:5/seg:0",
      "source": "System is loaded; scheduling latency > period",
      "source_hash": 10098168465015117166,
      "context_hash": 8113116050466817833,
      "translation": "시스템 부하가 높아 스케줄링 지연 시간 > 주기인 경우",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "latency": "지연 시간",
        "scheduling": "스케줄링"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T23:02:32.932511Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:5/block:6/seg:0",
      "source": "Thread was blocked (sleeping, waiting for I/O)",
      "source_hash": 8748588927372075466,
      "context_hash": 13087099415651544497,
      "translation": "스레드가 블록된 경우(sleep 중이거나 I/O 대기 중)",
